{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat","id":1043167,"title":"Can a mage evenly match a werewolf in melee or hand-to-hand combat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-03T14:59:56-08:00","id":1043167,"title":"Can a mage evenly match a werewolf in melee or hand-to-hand combat?","content":"Incoming stupid question ...<br /> <br /> To make things easier, let's say they're both of equal &quot;level,&quot; whatever that translates into.<br /> <br /> I figure if a mage (Adamantine Arrow) wanted they could specialize in melee combat and use all of their abilities to become Neo (the Matrix: Revolutions).<br /> <br /> However, I'm having trouble seeing how a mage could physically keep up with a werewolf if the goal is to match them in: strength, speed, life regen, etc. I'm not very knowledgeable in werewolf stuff, though.<br /> <br /> It seems as if a melee mage would just opt to incorporate melee-flavor into their spell-casting and just use spells that more or less mimic or approximate the things that a werewolf could do. Instead of throwing a car with raw strength, he might tap it and Force Push the vehicle (I know he doesn't need to.) Or instead of raw speed, he'll just use his brand of Celerity. Instead of life regen (or in addition to), use tons of damage mitigation that make him seem like he can go a few rounds in a boxing match with a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Anyone have an experience with this before? Any players that wanted to pummel a werewolf into paste on the wolf's terms? Anecdotal advice says a mage should plot from afar and engage only when certain of the outcome. Does this mean a mage and a werewolf could not go toe-to-toe gladiatorial arena style?<br /> <br /> Is this really difficult to do without committing a crapton of resources?<br /> <br /> I assume the main reason for a bunch of mechanical restraints is to keep the game lines sufficiently separate in playstyles. So if you want to be the strongest tank that ever was, you play Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Sidenote: When I think about it, Neo isn't really stronger. The physics of the matrix just succumb to his whim in a way that makes him appear absurdly powerful.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:06:06-08:00","id":1043171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat#post1043167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I'm having trouble seeing how a mage could physically keep up with a werewolf if the goal is to match them in: strength, speed, life regen, etc. I'm not very knowledgeable in werewolf stuff, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life Magic can get physical attributes to 10+, Mind Magic can do the same for skills.<br /> <br /> With enough Potency on Body Control, you can start regenerating similarly to a werewolf, but you can also flat heal yourself for ridiculous amounts of lethal with actual healing spells which renders regeneration mostly unnecessary.<br /> <br /> That said, if you want this stuff up a large portion of the time, it's a huge investment of resources (spell control).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:06:44-08:00","id":1043172,"title":"","content":"I guess for me the question is, why would a Mage want to get into a fight that doesn't play to their strengths? I think they could make themselves a decent challenge to a werewolf in a brawl, but &quot;cheating&quot; would be way easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:54:35-08:00","id":1043205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043171#post1043171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life Magic can get physical attributes to 10+, Mind Magic can do the same for skills.<br /> <br /> With enough Potency on Body Control, you can start regenerating similarly to a werewolf, but you can also flat heal yourself for ridiculous amounts of lethal with actual healing spells which renders regeneration mostly unnecessary.<br /> <br /> That said, if you want this stuff up a large portion of the time, it's a huge investment of resources (spell control).</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you set a bunch of these to be indefinite? Mages could dismantle it, but I don't know that werewolves could do the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:59:46-08:00","id":1043208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043172#post1043172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess for me the question is, why would a Mage want to get into a fight that doesn't play to their strengths? I think they could make themselves a decent challenge to a werewolf in a brawl, but &quot;cheating&quot; would be way easier.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just because they would like to. I realize the vast majority would prefer not to, but I always hear the premise that mages can more or less do whatever they want.<br /> <br /> If one of your goals is to best a werewolf at his own game, for whatever dingus reason, why not? (Aside from there being a myriad of better ways.)<br /> <br /> Let a mage dream.<br /> <br /> What I gather is that it is extremely taxing and werewolves would be mocking you for trying to fill shoes much too big for you, even if you could best them.<br /> <br /> Just as a curiosity, could a mage playing this sordid game of &quot;Beat you at your own&quot; defeat a werewolf if he uses all of his best abilities? (Again, assuming similar power levels.) I see Gauru form thrown around a lot and wonder if that would utterly decimate a mage even if they use Body Control and a bunch of other stuff to try and be on par.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:33:00-08:00","id":1043235,"title":"","content":"it's hard. Really hard. not impossible, but really really hard and pretty vulgar and reach demanding too. <br /> U probably need turn momentum (forces) with extra reaches to become immune to any physical attack from the giant wolf size enemy u are facing , set it to dodge as a reflexive action each turn. That should get u covered against fangs and brute strenght. Each time the werewolf tries to bite your throat, u simply dodge automatically.<br /> Then u probably need a forces effect (don't remember the exact rote but i think its forces 2 or 3) to power up your fists,, giving them lethal damage and set the potency high so they can deal 4-5 or more potency in damage each attack, then spend extra reaches so your attacks can produce the knocked down and stunned tilt BOTH.<br /> Now u have only with Forces a physically untouchable mage that can deal impressive damage with his bare hands.<br /> Only forces 3 required. Of course u are only going to &quot;almost&quot; match the werewolf and not actually gonna kill him, since he simply keeps regenerating all damage each turn. Also he can fuck u up with spirits and gifts.<br /> <br /> Now if u really want to build a werewolf hunter killing machine who can face a werewolf in a fight and probably win u need a thyrsus with forces or an obrimos with life and spirit. U need a high level mage, capable of dealing agg damage. 4 or 5 in the arcanas and high gnosis and mana...<br /> <br /> use turn momentum to dodge all physical attacks, t<br /> hen use spirit to shield yourself from numina, influence and gifts ( clash of wills)<br /> , use spirit to get yourself invisible to spirits and spirits perception powers,<br /> use Life to buff ur strenght and dexterity and stamina, and<br /> use forces to deal 4 to 5 or more agg damage with bare hands with both stunned and knocked down conditions on ur enemies. Thats a pretty bad enemy to face for a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Don't know about regenerating damage but u need at least life 4 or 5 to match werewolf regeneration imho.<br /> also time and fate are not bad at all.<br /> <br /> Use time acceleration to win the initiative or go for a clash of wills against the werewolf ability to interrupt other actions (wolf form, shapeshifting reflexive) , and use fate to gain 12+ dices on all your unarmed attacks, clash of wills or whatever.<br /> U can even give yourself a huge amount of bonus dices on your attacks and the 8 again too. Imagine a mage with 6+ strength, 5+ automatic aggr damage on his fists+ stunned and knocked down contidions each attack, and 10+ extra dices on all his attacks with reroll 8 on brawl.<br /> <br /> yep. That's pretty scary.<br /> <br /> But wolves have other ways to fight back too, gifts spirits allies fetishes...<br /> so i don't know -white rooms don't make too much sense as always. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> anyway i think i answered your question .)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:56:53-08:00","id":1043250,"title":"","content":"Yes, a skilled Mage knowledgeable in certain Arcana can enhance their own proficiency in various ways to reach a level that Werewolves can't achieve.<br /> However Mages can also cast many other kinds of spells which would render such a fight pointless (Ban springs to mind).<br /> <br /> Ultimately however, Mages are the planning and preptime faction. Give them time and resources and they can conquer most problems.<br /> Werewolves from character creation have a bevy of &quot;charge straight in and tear them a new one&quot; abilities.<br /> <br /> So yeah, in many circumstances, a Mage facing a suprise Garou straight out out of the blue is mincemeat.<br /> In many others, that Uratha finds himself &quot;trapped&quot; in a bubble of looped space until he runs out of air and dies<br /> <br /> The better question is why, how does it play into the story, and why would the character do so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:14:36-08:00","id":1043257,"title":"","content":"As has been said, they can, but it takes a bit of prep (like most things in mage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:25:04-08:00","id":1043262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043250#post1043250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, a skilled Mage knowledgeable in certain Arcana can enhance their own proficiency in various ways to reach a level that Werewolves can't achieve.<br /> However Mages can also cast many other kinds of spells which would render such a fight pointless (Ban springs to mind).<br /> <br /> Ultimately however, Mages are the planning and preptime faction. Give them time and resources and they can conquer most problems.<br /> Werewolves from character creation have a bevy of &quot;charge straight in and tear them a new one&quot; abilities.<br /> <br /> So yeah, in many circumstances, a Mage facing a suprise Garou straight out out of the blue is mincemeat.<br /> In many others, that Uratha finds himself &quot;trapped&quot; in a bubble of looped space until he runs out of air and dies<br /> <br /> The better question is why, how does it play into the story, and why would the character do so?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One example I can think of (for a particularly obsessed or mad mage) is to test the limits of magic (the idea that mages can do better in other less barbaric ways is in itself a challenge; &quot;We'll see about that.&quot;) In a more perverted sense, to replicated the werewolf splat or use some of its characteristics as a baseline to create an alleged &quot;superior&quot; specimen for undisclosed purposes.<br /> <br /> This might be a bonkers NPC. But it could also be something to experiment with, if only briefly, for a PC that wants to try and RP as Awakened Hulk.<br /> <br /> I see no problem if the rules clearly detail the drawbacks of pursuing such a whimsical endeavor. It also doesn't detract from the investigative/mystery aspects of mage, it just means that for whatever reason this mage likes to throw down with supernatural behemoths even if that means dying.<br /> <br /> My assumption is that if the mage sticks too blindly to their desires they will inevitably die at the hands of a wolf with more brains than the mage can sustain brawn.<br /> <br /> It was a question of whether or not they could, regardless of the likelihood of them bothering.<br /> <br /> I'm really amazed at how good some of you are and putting together spells on the fly.<br /> <br /> Is there a freaking exercise pamphlet or something? I'd love to be able to think of a thing I want to do and know instantly what Arcana I need to do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> If it is just practice then I guess I'll have to wait, as I have no way of playing mage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:27:32-08:00","id":1043263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043235#post1043235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's hard. Really hard. not impossible, but really really hard and pretty vulgar and reach demanding too.<br /> U probably need turn momentum (forces) with extra reaches to become immune to any physical attack from the giant wolf size enemy u are facing , set it to dodge as a reflexive action each turn. That should get u covered against fangs and brute strenght. Each time the werewolf tries to bite your throat, u simply dodge automatically.<br /> Then u probably need a forces effect (don't remember the exact rote but i think its forces 2 or 3) to power up your fists,, giving them lethal damage and set the potency high so they can deal 4-5 or more potency in damage each attack, then spend extra reaches so your attacks can produce the knocked down and stunned tilt BOTH.<br /> Now u have only with Forces a physically untouchable mage that can deal impressive damage with his bare hands.<br /> Only forces 3 required. Of course u are only going to &quot;almost&quot; match the werewolf and not actually gonna kill him, since he simply keeps regenerating all damage each turn. Also he can fuck u up with spirits and gifts.<br /> <br /> Now if u really want to build a werewolf hunter killing machine who can face a werewolf in a fight and probably win u need a thyrsus with forces or an obrimos with life and spirit. U need a high level mage, capable of dealing agg damage. 4 or 5 in the arcanas and high gnosis and mana...<br /> <br /> use turn momentum to dodge all physical attacks, t<br /> hen use spirit to shield yourself from numina, influence and gifts ( clash of wills)<br /> , use spirit to get yourself invisible to spirits and spirits perception powers,<br /> use Life to buff ur strenght and dexterity and stamina, and<br /> use forces to deal 4 to 5 or more agg damage with bare hands with both stunned and knocked down conditions on ur enemies. Thats a pretty bad enemy to face for a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Don't know about regenerating damage but u need at least life 4 or 5 to match werewolf regeneration imho.<br /> also time and fate are not bad at all.<br /> <br /> Use time acceleration to win the initiative or go for a clash of wills against the werewolf ability to interrupt other actions (wolf form, shapeshifting reflexive) , and use fate to gain 12+ dices on all your unarmed attacks, clash of wills or whatever.<br /> U can even give yourself a huge amount of bonus dices on your attacks and the 8 again too. Imagine a mage with 6+ strength, 5+ automatic aggr damage on his fists+ stunned and knocked down contidions each attack, and 10+ extra dices on all his attacks with reroll 8 on brawl.<br /> <br /> yep. That's pretty scary.<br /> <br /> But wolves have other ways to fight back too, gifts spirits allies fetishes...<br /> so i don't know -white rooms don't make too much sense as always. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> anyway i think i answered your question .)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for this response, this is more or less what I was looking for. I wish I could off-the-cuff know exactly how to build spells. It is a slow process for me to walk through!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:31:00-08:00","id":1043264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043262#post1043262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a freaking exercise pamphlet or something? I'd love to be able to think of a thing I want to do and know instantly what Arcana I need to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The practices section gives you the gist, then the spells section shows you what you're able to do, and gives you an idea of what you can do with other arcana.<br /> <br /> You might have a look at werewolf, too, since it's easy to get overconfident when you don't know the powers of the enemy. Space Bans are great but it would suck to rely on one and see the werewolf teleport out of it, or simply break it and inflict Berserk so you couldn't cast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it is just practice then I guess I'll have to wait, as I have no way of playing mage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>White room battles are silly, as it inevitably ends up with the kind of characters you would never see in a game in a situation you would never see in a game. But you might check out the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post\">Play by Post section of the forum</a>, as sometimes people recruit for games there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-03-2017, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:42:46-08:00","id":1043273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043264#post1043264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The practices section gives you the gist, then the spells section shows you what you're able to do, and gives you an idea of what you can do with other arcana.<br /> <br /> You might have a look at werewolf, too, since it's easy to get overconfident when you don't know the powers of the enemy. Space Bans are great but it would suck to rely on one and see the werewolf teleport out of it, or simply break it and inflict Berserk so you couldn't cast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> White room battles are silly, as it inevitably ends up with the kind of characters you would never see in a game in a situation you would never see in a game. But you might check out the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post\">Play by Post section of the forum</a>, as sometimes people recruit for games there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have the book but I haven't committed the practices and all they entail to memory. So I'm still blown away when I mention an effect and people come outta the woodwork to say how they would do it and there is no disagreement over it. It just works.<br /> <br /> Also, I must be retarded because I didn't check to see if there was Play-by-Post on this site. Thanks for the info!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:46:45-08:00","id":1043275,"title":"","content":"Neo is really the wrong example.<br /> <br /> You want Iron Man versus the Hulk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T18:01:47-08:00","id":1043281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043262#post1043262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a freaking exercise pamphlet or something? I'd love to be able to think of a thing I want to do and know instantly what Arcana I need to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the Practices and the Purviews in the rulebook.<br /> Combine one with the other, and look to the Creative Thaumaturgy section for advice.<br /> <br /> So say for instance you wanted to keep some sunlight in your pocket for a rainy day, or an aggressive Vampire.<br /> You could either use Force 4 to Pattern Sunlight into behaving like a tangible object for as long as you want, allowing you to literally bundle it up and keep it in your pocket.<br /> Or Matter 4 to change the properties of, say for instance, a Glass sphere to contain light until you need it based entire on refraction.<br /> <br /> Or say you wanted to transform say... A Vampire into a Chair. That would require Patterning to completely change something under the spell's purview, and since you're modifying a Corpse into an inanimate object, you'd need that much in Death and Matter. So Death 4, Matter 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T19:23:42-08:00","id":1043314,"title":"","content":"Its actually pretty easy. Kinetic Blow with enough Potency and a good weapon can deal enough damage to kill someone in Gauru in a single hit. Armor, defense boosts and mage armor can keep the magus alive. Superlative Luck or Destiny can ensure a hit.<br /> <br /> The key is that the mage would need to have these spells prepared, and the appropriate mage armor up. That generally requires having time outside of combat to prep the Yantra and possibly use an extended cast ritual. <br /> <br /> This comes down to the same refrain, really. A mage who has the time to prepare will generally succeed in any encounter. A mage who's caught off guard or blind sided is generally in trouble. Chances are, any given Arrow is not going to have these spells and the appropriate defenses prepped to take on a Rahu werewolf. Even if they had all the spells ready, the sudden appearance of something unexpected (lets just say a promethean for the hell of it), means that the mage is basically easy bait for that promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T19:34:08-08:00","id":1043319,"title":"","content":"THe notion that a mage should be able to go toe to toe with a werewolf is nonsense perpetuated by the idea that a Mage, because of the flexibility of their capabilities, can do anything that the other splats can. Technically, that's true, but that doesn't encapsulate what a mage does best, no matter what the supremacists might suggest.<br /> <br /> A Mage trying to fight on a werewolf's terms is losing that fight. A Mage does better with long-planned, high-scale escalation in terms of response. A mage who tries to match his peers on the in-the-fly moments might <i>barely</i> catch up, which makes it all the worse when a werewolf breaks out their gifts and ruin whatever the fuck the mage thought was good and possible in the moment. A mage in those cases is better off stalling until they can run or until a fellow pulls a fucking rabbit out of the hat;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-03-2017, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T20:41:08-08:00","id":1043345,"title":"","content":"I'm not a Werewolf fan, so I don't know what are their capabilities, but Obrimos is probably the safest bet for aspiring martial artist - both Werewolf punching and generally punching. Their Arcana spread makes sustaining a lot of buffs easily, as Dispel Magic allows them to safely unsafely release spells, as long as they Dispel them before they go sour. This takes at least a day, so Obrimos Kung Fu Puncher can pretty much keep them indefinietely ,and incorporate dispelling and recasting them into their morning martial arts routine, which is a boon in terms of flavor and reinforcing your magical identity. This pretty much makes problem of having to manage spell control irrelevant, so Obrimos who dedicates themselves to be always ready for physical conflict - which sounds like something an Arrow would do - is limited less by their resources, and more by their imagination and Arcana. By bypassing the spell control limitation, they can preemptively cover any angle of attack, as long as they can both think of it and get proper dot ratings to do so. And luckily, Forces is really good about optimizing physical performance while also turning yourself pretty much invincible to being damaged by impact, energy and other typical forms of damage. So if you want to punch werewolves, get Prime 1, some Forces, and 2 or 1 dots in stuff that can protect you from non-physical means of werewolf attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T20:48:04-08:00","id":1043349,"title":"","content":"If a Rahu hits the mage with their Hunter Aspect they're decidedly fucked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:16:05-08:00","id":1043362,"title":"","content":"When it comes to comparing Mages to other supernatural splats in that splat's area of strength I use the airplane vs bird analogy. A man can fly faster, higher, farther and longer than any bird can dream of doing, as long as he has a plane. On the other hand all the bird needs to fly is open sky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:24:33-08:00","id":1043368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043349#post1043349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Rahu hits the mage with their Hunter Aspect they're decidedly fucked.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would have to succeed and not be removed by a mage after a turn.<br /> <br /> The fights impossible to white room. You have so many werewolves and so many mage builds it's impossible to tell.<br /> <br /> Physically purely physically a mage would have to load up with life and and forces spells. Life spells to increase you own attack give yourself aggravated fist damage and decrease their str and dex values to compete. Forces to maximize attack as well as repel. The issue then becomes everything else that gets thrown out which also requires mind and spirit to combat. Mages and werewolves do the same thing completely differently It's really not a question of if a mage can match and/or power a werewolf but rather how much experience and preparation. The answer to these questions is too much and a lot. You'd be better off just taking spirit and completely fucking a werewolf with an army of spirits than you would getting that much life/forces/mind to deal with him otherwise. If you do find yourself in a fight you'd be better off using mind to confuse him or space get to a vantage point. But only time you'd stand a chance is if you had life and forces spells already up. However thing about games that use rng is the fact that the dice could go entirely in your favor.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:25:16-08:00","id":1043370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043349#post1043349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Rahu hits the mage with their Hunter Aspect they're decidedly fucked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is it a done deal? I'm not familiar with werewolf, so I'm curious.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:29:34-08:00","id":1043373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043370#post1043370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is it a done deal? I'm not familiar with werewolf, so I'm curious.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It give them a pretty annoying condition to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:38:49-08:00","id":1043377,"title":"","content":"It causes the target to become overconfident. It's aptly named Swaggering.<br /> <br /> Werewolf, p311. 'Your character faced the full bore of a Rahu\u2019s essence. He\u2019s sure that he can win in the face of the Rahu\u2019s fury. He can not prepare himself to face the Rahu or her pack in any way \u2014 buying weapons, laying traps, or changing his normal routine \u2014 without first spending a Willpower point and making an extended, reflexive Resolve + Composure roll. You may make one roll per turn, but each roll requires an additional point of Willpower. The target number of successes is equal to the Rahu\u2019s Purity.'<br /> <br /> Basically, no prep time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:40:22-08:00","id":1043378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043345#post1043345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not a Werewolf fan, so I don't know what are their capabilities, but Obrimos is probably the safest bet for aspiring martial artist - both Werewolf punching and generally punching. Their Arcana spread makes sustaining a lot of buffs easily, as Dispel Magic allows them to safely unsafely release spells, as long as they Dispel them before they go sour. This takes at least a day, so Obrimos Kung Fu Puncher can pretty much keep them indefinietely ,and incorporate dispelling and recasting them into their morning martial arts routine, which is a boon in terms of flavor and reinforcing your magical identity. This pretty much makes problem of having to manage spell control irrelevant, so Obrimos who dedicates themselves to be always ready for physical conflict - which sounds like something an Arrow would do - is limited less by their resources, and more by their imagination and Arcana. By bypassing the spell control limitation, they can preemptively cover any angle of attack, as long as they can both think of it and get proper dot ratings to do so. And luckily, Forces is really good about optimizing physical performance while also turning yourself pretty much invincible to being damaged by impact, energy and other typical forms of damage. So if you want to punch werewolves, get Prime 1, some Forces, and 2 or 1 dots in stuff that can protect you from non-physical means of werewolf attack.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Forces seems like it should dish out and absorb a lot of what a werewolf could put out in purely physical respect.<br /> <br /> <b>(To certain respondents [not you, WHW]) ******I acknowledge, and continue to acknowledge, and will continue to acknowledge that:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Werewolves have a plethora of abilities at their disposal and can do many interesting things with those abilities.<br /> 2) Mages are better off using OTHER means to deal with a fight against a werewolf and that a mage would be SEVERELY LIMITING themselves if they chose to go about it in a &quot;purely physical&quot; battle (the mage would essentially still be cheating by making a human husk into something it is clearly not.)<br /> 3) That white room battles, such as this, are pointless if you're going to weigh things down with all the contextual trappings that usually come with encountering a werewolf in a game setting with a typical mage character.<br /> <br /> That said, I did note that the comparison was more of a mechanical intrigue. The enemy does not need to be a werewolf, it could be something comparable in a physical sense.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;flavor-text&quot; or the &quot;why&quot; of it all, it is largely irrelevant, as that is up to a prospective ST.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason I stopped posting as frequently on these forums is the pressure that comes with asking purely speculative questions like this. I got plenty of really awesome responses [citing what you would need; ignoring the absurdity of it all and just answering the question via game mechanics that do permit it], but I also get a bunch of responses that don't care what the mechanics are and just can't rationalize why this would be a curiosity or ever be relevant. The latter responses often won't even make an attempt to answer the question and just want to comment on the ridiculousness of it all.<br /> <br /> I don't get it. :\\ Why comment at all, then?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I really appreciate the variety of responses coming from those that essentially have come to the open consensus that it would be taxing, foolhardy, strenuous, but do-able.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":11166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","user":"kryptonitekrusher","date":". 02-04-2017, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:52:33-08:00","id":1043381,"title":"","content":"It's kind of a weird question, especially if you open it up to other things. But it's the sort of thing that comes up a lot. Yes, mages can fight in melee, some of their artifact weapons are incredibly powerful too and they have spells that can enhance their abilities. They can also learn Fighting Styles and Brawl and Weaponry with the rest of people.<br /> <br /> I had an interesting combat scene when a Beast attacked a group of three mages. She really hurt them pretty badly, and they had been burdened down with Conditions and Tilts that basically gave them no chance to really do anything. They had been prepared but not incredibly, only having their armor and a couple other non-related spells on. One was knocked out of the fight instantly, the Beast's Looming Presence inflicted the Beaten Down Condition, so she ended up just using boons on the other two. The Beast had created a snowstorm and deafened them but with the boon and another spell to add Firearms skill they managed to take the Beast down. She was a Merger, a Rampant Beast that didn't have Lair. If she did she probably would have killed someone. Not sure if you have the book but her stats were based on Starless, p241, though some were changed a bit.<br /> <br /> If she played it more smart, as well, but she wasn't aware they were coming and was being driven mad by an Aggressive Meme. If the mages were alone, they would have died, at least if they kept fighting. At least two of them would have been able to just get away, which would have been more likely than standing out there and fighting to the death with a giant bird monster.<br /> <br /> Just the way the game is made, once you start going cross-splat, it's really hard to say anyone is even against anyone else, the powers are so different, even the innate abilities are game changers, which is more to the point of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-04-2017, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T22:30:10-08:00","id":1043390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043381#post1043381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's kind of a weird question, especially if you open it up to other things. Yes, mages can fight in melee, some of their artifact weapons are incredibly powerful too and they have spells that can enhance their abilities. They can also learn Fighting Styles and Brawl and Weaponry with the rest of people.<br /> <br /> I had an interesting combat scene when a Beast attacked a group of three mages. She really hurt them pretty badly, and they had been burdened down with Conditions and Tilts that basically gave them no chance to really do anything. They had been prepared but not incredibly, only having their armor and a couple other non-related spells on. One was knocked out of the fight instantly, the Beast's Looming Presence inflicted the Beaten Down Condition, so she ended up just using boons on the other two. The Beast had created a snowstorm and deafened them but with the boon and another spell to add Firearms skill they managed to take the Beast down. She was a Merger, a Rampant Beast that didn't have Lair. If she did she probably would have killed someone. Not sure if you have the book but her stats were based on Starless, p241, though some were changed a bit.<br /> <br /> If she played it more smart, as well, but she wasn't aware they were coming and was being driven mad by an Aggressive Meme. If the mages were alone, they would have died, at least if they kept fighting. At least two of them would have been able to just get away, which would have been more likely than standing out there and fighting to the death with a giant bird monster.<br /> <br /> Just the way the game is made, once you start going cross-splat, it's really hard to say anyone is even against anyone else, the powers are so different, even the innate abilities are game changers, which is more to the point of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it serves as a good example for why you play any given splat, to say the least.<br /> <br /> Similarly, you could probably play a mage that operates like a vampire, but from what I've read a mage's powers don't have the same certainty that Disciplines do; at least not until you have the resources to safely relinquish things left and right.<br /> <br /> Also, I've not played Beast. I must confess that I actually own Forsaken/Requiem/Descent/and Awakening. But 100% of my focus has been on absorbing Mage the Awakening. I plan to get all titles eventually, since I think CoD is a really awesome universe and the first tabletop experience I've ever really enjoyed.<br /> <br /> If I could use Time (would that be Ruling? Weaving? Making?) to give myself longer days, I would at least think very seriously about committing the rest of my collection to memory. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T23:44:13-08:00","id":1043399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043377#post1043377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It causes the target to become overconfident. It's aptly named Swaggering.<br /> <br /> Werewolf, p311. 'Your character faced the full bore of a Rahu\u2019s essence. He\u2019s sure that he can win in the face of the Rahu\u2019s fury. He can not prepare himself to face the Rahu or her pack in any way \u2014 buying weapons, laying traps, or changing his normal routine \u2014 without first spending a Willpower point and making an extended, reflexive Resolve + Composure roll. You may make one roll per turn, but each roll requires an additional point of Willpower. The target number of successes is equal to the Rahu\u2019s Purity.'<br /> <br /> Basically, no prep time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'd just spend the Willpower and prep anyways. I mean with a mages praxis, they can pretty much replenish their Willpower at will as part of said prep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T23:48:43-08:00","id":1043400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043399#post1043399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I'd just spend the Willpower and prep anyways. I mean with a mages praxis, they can pretty much replenish their Willpower at will as part of said prep.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Spend Willpower and extended roll* - admittedly the target isn't huge but success isn't guaranteed. Also consider, if the Rahu has been close enough to place the Hunter's Aspect on you, it's coming for the you during those turns.<br /> <br /> But as has been said many times before, and several in this thread, white room scenarios are rather pointless as they don't take into account even a fraction of the required variables.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T23:55:23-08:00","id":1043401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043400#post1043400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *Spend Willpower and extended roll* - admittedly the target isn't huge but success isn't guaranteed. Also consider, if the Rahu has been close enough to place the Hunter's Aspect on you, it's coming for the you during those turns.<br /> <br /> But as has been said many times before, and several in this thread, white room scenarios are rather pointless as they don't take into account even a fraction of the required variables.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if that were the case you probably wouldn't have much time to prep regardless. Which is why I'd probably just retreat/make distance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T00:11:35-08:00","id":1043403,"title":"","content":"Depends on what you mean by 'on their own terms'. A Mage would be hard pressed to become a more vicious, rapid healing murder machine than a Werewolf in Gauru (though, if I had to try it'd probably involve Life, Forces, and Time with lots of hung healing spells). However, if you merely mean to beat the wolf in a mostly straight up hand-to-hand fight. Yes, a Mage can absolutely do this.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the Mage will need to be a little purpose built, but there are plenty of spell and style combinations that can make a Mage terrific in close combat. Just a pair from a recent thread (the supernatural fighting style thread):<ul><li>A mage with Acceleration and the third dot of Armed Defense can hike their defense to preposterous levels (like 50+ dice) which can then be converted into damage against anyone who attacks them. Get a scene long casting of Present as Past up to negate any form of surprise, and put Sands of Time on Rote to reset if things go south. Then get some spirit to deal with the Shadow side of Werewolf and you've got a strong contender.</li> <li>Mages can achieve absolutely ridiculous ratings for Armor and Weapon enhancements.Between Matter 3 and Prime 3 a mage can perfect tools to an absolutely staggering degree. 10 points of Armor and +10 Weapons are not out of the question. They also find it trivially easy to overcome a Werewolf's regeneration (both Prime and Matter can achieve this). It takes a damn well spec'd Werewolf to survive close combat with numbers like that.</li> </ul>Now this is not to say that Mages will kick a werewolf's ass, nor that Werewolves don't have tools and means to defeat the above examples. We could go back and forth about what trumps what forever, literally. I'm just saying, yeah, Werewolves aren't uncontested at the top of the fighty pile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T01:09:38-08:00","id":1043413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043401#post1043401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if that were the case you probably wouldn't have much time to prep regardless. Which is why I'd probably just retreat/make distance.</div> </div> </div> </div>'He's sure that he can win in the face of the Rahu's fury.'<br /> <br /> Running away to prepare is still preparing. There's no reason to not fight the Rahu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-04-2017, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T02:02:58-08:00","id":1043424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043413#post1043413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'He's sure that he can win in the face of the Rahu's fury.'<br /> <br /> Running away to prepare is still preparing. There's no reason to not fight the Rahu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yo first have to lose a roll if you spend willpower it's not oncontested and have several ways out. Also a mind mage can remove conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T03:08:57-08:00","id":1043440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043413#post1043413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'He's sure that he can win in the face of the Rahu's fury.'<br /> <br /> Running away to prepare is still preparing. There's no reason to not fight the Rahu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Running away to reposition is just a part of the fight, it isn't prep. Just because you can't prepare beforehand doesn't mean you have to be stupid mid-fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 02-04-2017, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T03:35:47-08:00","id":1043448,"title":"","content":"If it's a Mental Condition, then any Mage can Pattern Restore it away. Question is, of course, if you are feeling the need to do so in the first place!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T04:04:14-08:00","id":1043455,"title":"","content":"Ran some numbers just for funsies. Only using published spells because honestly, Creative Thaumaturgy makes this way too easy.<br /> <br /> You can hit 10 in every physical attribute plus the relevant combat skills with 3 combined spells. These are going to need to be ritually cast, and you're going to have to be a Disciple of Life and Mind, but it's totally doable assuming you have 3 in the relevant traits beforehand.<br /> This is going to give you 15 health, an average of 12 defense (20 if you enhance wits to the same degree, but that's an extra spell control slot, you could combine it with enhancing Resolve for an average WP pool of 12).<br /> <br /> <br /> What's not going to be doable reasonably is the regeneration. You'd need 19 Potency to regen one lethal per turn with Body Control, although every point of Potency above and beyond that is going to have <i>massive </i>returns. To even have a hope of doing this, you can forget being a Disciple - you want Mastery for the free Potency.<br /> <br /> Change the Primary Factor, and you knock the number of 'additional' Potency you need down to...14. That's -28 dice. Even assuming you can deploy 4 yantras, You're looking at, at best, +4 Persona, +2 High Speech, +2 Runes, +5 Rote. That's only +13 Dice, and after factoring in Gnosis 6 and Life 5 you're still 4 dice in the hole. Ritually casting it brings your total dice up to...1. Spend willpower, and you can get a respectable 4 dice.<br /> <br /> Except if you want it to last any reasonable amount of time, you're still going to need to add a bit of Duration. Making it last a day is going to cost you two dice, for a final dicepool of two, which fails more often than it succeeds.<br /> <br /> <b>tl;dr</b> while adding massive numbers to mundane combat dice pools is super easy, matching one of the most basic features of the Forsaken template requires Mastery and hours of ritually casting and still doesn't get results reliably.<br /> <br /> And it still doesn't hold a candle to Gauru regen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T04:05:52-08:00","id":1043456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043440#post1043440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running away to reposition is just a part of the fight, it isn't prep. Just because you can't prepare beforehand doesn't mean you have to be stupid mid-fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a werewolf Hunting Aspect. Making the prey stupid for the fight is exactly its purpose. <br /> <br /> To give the OP an answer which I find is generally most useful - it depends on the protagonist. Or, in practice:<br /> <br /> Q - Can a mage evenly match a werewolf in melee or hand-to-hand?<br /> <br /> A1 - In a Mage game? Probably.<br /> A2 - In a Werewolf game? Not likely.<br /> A3 - In a mixed game? Who's the protagonist? Refer to A1 and A2 above.<br /> A4 - In player vs player? Whomever has the better strategy and uses the environment best. This isn't a white room.<br /> A5 - In NPC vs NPC? Whichever most dramatically suits the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T04:22:48-08:00","id":1043460,"title":"","content":"I think its also relevant to discuss that no Arrow in their right mind would want to match a werewolf in a straight up fight outside of some formalized duel for some story reason (and the duel would probably hamstring said mage in other ways).<br /> <br /> &quot;Adaptability is Strength.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is a core tenant of the Arrows. You don't want to overload your spell limits with matching a werewolf, and leaving yourself open in new ways. You would want to prepare your defenses in such a way that you can survive what the wolf deals out, and then be able to respond with physical or magical actions as needed, depending on what's happening. Who needs to take a risk of a werewolf bringing a fetish gun to a fist fight when they could just as easily have one's own spell gun to snipe with, or lock the opponent in a ward, or curse the opponent into impotency? Or, more relevantly, be able to do all of the above depending on the situation?<br /> <br /> Mages and werewolves each have their own specialties. If you want to be good, even at white room dueling, you should play to your splat's strengths. Hunting, shapeshifting, and fear inducements for the wolves, information gathering, defenses and flexibility for mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-04-2017, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T04:27:20-08:00","id":1043462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043448#post1043448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's a Mental Condition, then any Mage can Pattern Restore it away. Question is, of course, if you are feeling the need to do so in the first place!</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, where does it say that pattern restoration cures status effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T04:39:40-08:00","id":1043469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043462#post1043462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um, where does it say that pattern restoration cures status effects?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the Pattern Restoration. <br /> &quot;Pattern Restoration: as an instant action, a mage can bolster her Pattern and heal mentally or physically. Three Mana points can heal a level of bashing or lethal damage. Alternatively, the <br /> mage can remove a Mental Condition (this does not offer a Beat) or a Physical Tilt.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T05:56:44-08:00","id":1043499,"title":"","content":"Probably the lowest investment way to fight a werewolf is to maximize your chances of dodging and have Mind or Space Mage Armor up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T06:07:17-08:00","id":1043504,"title":"","content":"I probably would fight a werewolf by sending a bunch of illusions after it, wait until Gauru time runs out, then snipe at leisure. If the wolf falls into Death Rage instead, get your ass out of there, keep civvies away, and wait for Death Rage to wear off. Then create an illusion of a slaughter, wait for werewolf to break down in tears at the carnage, and shoot him in the back of the head, coup de grace rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T06:24:04-08:00","id":1043509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043504#post1043504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably would fight a werewolf by sending a bunch of illusions after it, wait until Gauru time runs out, then snipe at leisure. If the wolf falls into Death Rage instead, get your ass out of there, keep civvies away, and wait for Death Rage to wear off. Then create an illusion of a slaughter, wait for werewolf to break down in tears at the carnage, and shoot him in the back of the head, coup de grace rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just throw a couple high potency agg spells, personally.<br /> Killing anything vulnerable to aggravated damage is trivial for an Adept, excepting circumstances where they get instantly killed before they can cast or where they can't perceive their target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T06:29:19-08:00","id":1043511,"title":"","content":"Funny thing is we are arguing about a mage going in toe.to.toe in a brawl fight against a werewolf _ the field where werewolves are absolutely the apex predators with their gifts regeneration and damage pools/ but a simple young obrimos or a mastigos can create havoc to an entire pack of.werewolves simply by changing the gravity (forces) or using.a.mind.domination spell with extra reaches to.command 2 or 3 members of the pack to.&quot;fight eachother&quot; or &quot;defend me&quot;....<br /> Just laugh as the puppetter while the wolves are.flying up in the air hopelessly or they start tearing each other apart. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not to mention u can simply use a space 3 Ban and close a werewolf in a prison he cannot escape unless he has special gifts or fetishes.<br /> <br /> But yeah i dont think overall its a good idea to go fight a werewolf bare handed werwwolves have gifts and aspects too/ butchery from the rahu list and relentless assault style,anyone? The rahu can simply cause the arm or.leg wreck just because u tried to touch him. 0.o","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T06:29:39-08:00","id":1043512,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm assuming starting characters, not Adapts. Agg damage does change things quite a bit, but anyone can do agg with a silver weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T12:10:53-08:00","id":1043669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043456#post1043456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a werewolf Hunting Aspect. Making the prey stupid for the fight is exactly its purpose.<br /> <br /> To give the OP an answer which I find is generally most useful - it depends on the protagonist. Or, in practice:<br /> <br /> Q - Can a mage evenly match a werewolf in melee or hand-to-hand?<br /> <br /> A1 - In a Mage game? Probably.<br /> A2 - In a Werewolf game? Not likely.<br /> A3 - In a mixed game? Who's the protagonist? Refer to A1 and A2 above.<br /> A4 - In player vs player? Whomever has the better strategy and uses the environment best. This isn't a white room.<br /> A5 - In NPC vs NPC? Whichever most dramatically suits the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>But unless there is more to that specific Aspect that wasn't posted, it doesn't make them stupid in this particular way. They can't prepare for a fight, but once the fight breaks out it is no longer preparing. After that point, you're just fighting, and movement (even tactical magical movement) is a part of fighting.<br /> <br /> Also, I would think that there'd be a decent chance of a Mage showing up in a werewolf game that can handle itself just as well in melee, I mean big name antagonists should be able to pull off some crazy stuff from time to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 02-04-2017, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T13:09:01-08:00","id":1043697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043455#post1043455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ran some numbers just for funsies. Only using published spells because honestly, Creative Thaumaturgy makes this way too easy.<br /> <br /> You can hit 10 in every physical attribute plus the relevant combat skills with 3 combined spells. These are going to need to be ritually cast, and you're going to have to be a Disciple of Life and Mind, but it's totally doable assuming you have 3 in the relevant traits beforehand.<br /> This is going to give you 15 health, an average of 12 defense (20 if you enhance wits to the same degree, but that's an extra spell control slot, you could combine it with enhancing Resolve for an average WP pool of 12).<br /> <br /> <br /> What's not going to be doable reasonably is the regeneration. You'd need 19 Potency to regen one lethal per turn with Body Control, although every point of Potency above and beyond that is going to have <i>massive </i>returns. To even have a hope of doing this, you can forget being a Disciple - you want Mastery for the free Potency.<br /> <br /> Change the Primary Factor, and you knock the number of 'additional' Potency you need down to...14. That's -28 dice. Even assuming you can deploy 4 yantras, You're looking at, at best, +4 Persona, +2 High Speech, +2 Runes, +5 Rote. That's only +13 Dice, and after factoring in Gnosis 6 and Life 5 you're still 4 dice in the hole. Ritually casting it brings your total dice up to...1. Spend willpower, and you can get a respectable 4 dice.<br /> <br /> Except if you want it to last any reasonable amount of time, you're still going to need to add a bit of Duration. Making it last a day is going to cost you two dice, for a final dicepool of two, which fails more often than it succeeds.<br /> <br /> <b>tl;dr</b> while adding massive numbers to mundane combat dice pools is super easy, matching one of the most basic features of the Forsaken template requires Mastery and hours of ritually casting and still doesn't get results reliably.<br /> <br /> And it still doesn't hold a candle to Gauru regen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the system is beautiful for having ways to accomplish this feat. Also, your (and many others) number crunching really helps to show some perspective. The sheer dice accounting is enough to keep most sensible mages away (conserving resources; getting the most bang for your buck; striking when the time is right; element of surprise, etc.)<br /> <br /> Some other solutions listed are off-the-cuff solutions to give a werewolf the impression their opponent isn't squishy. These snappy solutions are probably more akin to what a mage under surprise attack would do and I can readily appreciate them as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T13:21:01-08:00","id":1043703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043378#post1043378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the reason I stopped posting as frequently on these forums is the pressure that comes with asking purely speculative questions like this. I got plenty of really awesome responses [citing what you would need; ignoring the absurdity of it all and just answering the question via game mechanics that do permit it], but I also get a bunch of responses that don't care what the mechanics are and just can't rationalize why this would be a curiosity or ever be relevant. The latter responses often won't even make an attempt to answer the question and just want to comment on the ridiculousness of it all.<br /> <br /> I don't get it. :\\ Why comment at all, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you should have named your thread, &quot;Absurd white room speculation: Mages pretending to be Werewolves in the name of trying to perform mental contortions wherein OPP as a whole is a single game product but with splats as classes&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, at some point, after spending enough time on a forum, you should realize that no one reads the OP if they have a response to the thread title.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T14:29:28-08:00","id":1043733,"title":"","content":"Ran some numbers of my own on a couple previous approaches, restricting myself to victory through melee damage (as opposed to floating the enemy in the air and blasting them in a leisurely manner). Same disclaimer applies, these aren't guaranteed kill alls, they have weaknesses and can be overcome. And no build survives contact with the plot. However all three fare extremely well in CQC vs a Werewolf, even one spec'd for combat, and would make menacing antagonists for a Forsaken game.<br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enter the Dragon (Acanthus, Gnosis 4)</span></span></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Attributes</b>: Dexterity 5, Wits 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Skills</b>: Weaponry 5 (Nunchucks)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Merits</b>: Armed Defense 4, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Fighting Finesse, Adamant Hand (Weaponry), </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shadow Name 3 (The Dragon)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Arcana</b>: Time 4, Fate 3, Spirit 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Rotes</b>: Acceleration, Monkey's Paw, Shifting Sands</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Strategy</b>: Before combat the Mage precasts a really high potency Monkey's Paw on the weapon of her choice, let's go full Enter the Dragon and use nunchucks. She bumps the weapon bonus up to +10 and make this last at least 24 hours (indefinite might be better). Next she casts Acceleration with a high potency, lets say 10 . She'll add the extra reach to make all Dodge actions Rote while she's at it. Now the Mage's Dodge pool is ~40 dice, 30 vs Gauru. This can be bumped to 60 (50 vs Gauru) with dot 4 of Armed Defense turning her weapon bonus into a defense bonus. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit 2 is there to grant vision of spirits, and the ability to answer Numina if necessary. Shifting Sands is there to bug out if things get hairy and do a fight reset. For extra safety the Mage can hang a casting of Temporal Summoning to restore her to peak condition if she's struck, or cast Past as Present in turn 1 and foresee everything her opponent(s) is going to do.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Combat is mostly spent waiting for her opponent(s) to line up for a good attack. Starting with Present as Past guarantees she'll know what the Werewolf (or pack) is planning, and gives her the means to answer it. When the time is right she uses dot 3 of Armed Defense to turn her Dodge pool into a counter attack. With Rote Quality she can expect damage returns in the range of 20+ successes. Enough to pour past most Werewolves lethal track and begin to deal aggravated damage.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Iron Man (Obrimos, Gnosis 3)</span></span></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Attributes</b>: Strength 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Skills</b>: Weaponry 5 (Poleaxe)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Merits</b>: Heavy Weaponry 4, Defensive Combat, Adamant Hand (Weaponry), </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shadow Name 3 (Iron Man)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Arcana</b>: Matter 3, Force 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Rotes</b>: Kinetic Blow, Aegis</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Strategy</b>: First, become Iron Man. The Mage gets himself a suit of full body armor and uses matter to reshape it such that it has zero openings, then casts Aegis to give it a huge armor rating. 10 is fairly doable. Next get a big weapon, a poleaxe will do, he casts Kinetic Blow to boost its weapon bonus to +10, also use some reach so it stuns and knocks down on every hit. He makes the weapon silver while he's at it too. Now he's headed to combat with 10 Armor and +10 Damage, but it gets better. With Heavy Weapons 4 the Mage can use that weapon bonus as yet further armor, hiking that value up to 20 (without sacrificing the damage). With Armor that high he can afford to take risks until he knocks down or stun the Werewolf, from there it\u2019s pure beating with a +10 Silver weapon.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Rawr I'm a Dinosaur (Thrysis, Gnosis 4)</u></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Attributes</b>: Whatever, he's turning into a dinosaur</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Skills</b>: Brawl 5 (Megaraptor)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Merits</b>: Relentless Assault 4, Techne (Jurassic Park), Shadow Name 3 (Megaraptor)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Arcana</b>: Life 4, Mind 3, Death 2, Time 2, Spirit 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Rotes</b>: Shapechange, Hone the Form, Enhance Skills, Mend</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Strategy</b>: Start by turning into a megaraptor, gaining all it's presumably high attributes, natural weapons, and dinoness. Next hike physical attributes and Brawl as high as possible. Assuming Gnosis 4, Life 4, Rote +5, High Speech +2, Persona +4, Legacy Yantra +2 he'll be looking at a dice pool of 19 dice, willpower takes it to 22. One could reasonably boost attributes to +5 across the board, albeit the roll is dicey so he'll want to give himself the steadfast condition to guarantee success. Mind 3 can achieve that. Brawl &amp; Wits needs to be boosted similarly, which is entirely doable. He'll be out a bunch of mana and willpower by the end of the process, but has the joy of being a superpowered magical dinosaur.<br /> End result looks something like: Attack - 25 dice, Defense - 20 (10 against Gauru), Health - 18...which still doesn't look great matched up against Gauru. To turn the tide he'll need Mend, cast with high potency hung with Time. Death Armor will also help, effectively doubling his health track by converting everything to bashing. Finally Relentless Assault lets him make huge all-out attacks without losing defense, and grants a little boost to damage and armor. </span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Between the three builds I'd give best odds to The Dragon, mostly because it leverages highly magey tactics for which Werewolves have very few answers (fucking with time and being precognizant). Of all of them she's probably the best suited to beat more than one Werewolf at a time. Iron Man is insanely dangerous to Werewolves as well, but slightly more prone to being caught out on a weakness he doesn't have covered (for instance, if his Armor can be negated for even a single attack he's in trouble), but if the pack doesn't have a solution to his armor Iron Man will be essentially invulnerable. Dinosaur is closest to the original question, and can win, but I still feel one more Arcana (probably Fate or Forces) would be needed to tip the advantage to the Mage. However, it's key to note that in all three cases the Mage is dumping major time, mana, and willpower into the fight and relying on tools ritually prepared well in advance. A Werewolf can be a ripping, killing machine at the drop of a hat.<br /> <br /> Verdict: Mages can win in CQC, but they have to be built for it. However, a Mage built for CQC can be an unholy terror on par with even the fightiest of other splats. Conversely werewolves will dominate in CQC even with very little investment. Indeed one has to purposefully build away from combat to make a Werewolf bad at CQC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-04-2017, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T16:22:44-08:00","id":1043762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043703#post1043703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you should have named your thread, &quot;Absurd white room speculation: Mages pretending to be Werewolves in the name of trying to perform mental contortions wherein OPP as a whole is a single game product but with splats as classes&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, at some point, after spending enough time on a forum, you should realize that no one reads the OP if they have a response to the thread title.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I prefaced the initial post with &quot;Incoming stupid question ...&quot; as a way to acknowledge that it was absurd already. I think my question is straight forward enough. The title reads &quot;Can ...&quot; as in &quot;is it a thing that a mage CAN do.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not a question of &quot;is it a thing a mage WOULD do.&quot;<br /> <br /> The whole act of coming in just to remark on the absurdity of it, when it has already been recognized as that, is redundant and doesn't help the OP.<br /> <br /> It's just &quot;hurhur&quot;ing for the sake of it. I debated whether or not to post the question because I knew I would draw out people that had criticisms of the question on its face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T16:42:10-08:00","id":1043769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043733#post1043733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ran some numbers of my own on a couple previous approaches, restricting myself to victory through melee damage (as opposed to floating the enemy in the air and blasting them in a leisurely manner). Same disclaimer applies, these aren't guaranteed kill alls, they have weaknesses and can be overcome. And no build survives contact with the plot. However all three fare extremely well in CQC vs a Werewolf, even one spec'd for combat, and would make menacing antagonists for a Forsaken game.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Between the three builds I'd give best odds to The Dragon, mostly because it leverages highly magey tactics for which Werewolves have very few answers (fucking with time and being precognizant). Of all of them she's probably the best suited to beat more than one Werewolf at a time. Iron Man is insanely dangerous to Werewolves as well, but slightly more prone to being caught out on a weakness he doesn't have covered (for instance, if his Armor can be negated for even a single attack he's in trouble), but if the pack doesn't have a solution to his armor Iron Man will be essentially invulnerable. Dinosaur is closest to the original question, and can win, but I still feel one more Arcana (probably Fate or Forces) would be needed to tip the advantage to the Mage. However, it's key to note that in all three cases the Mage is dumping major time, mana, and willpower into the fight and relying on tools ritually prepared well in advance. A Werewolf can be a ripping, killing machine at the drop of a hat.<br /> <br /> Verdict: Mages can win in CQC, but they have to be built for it. However, a Mage built for CQC can be an unholy terror on par with even the fightiest of other splats. Conversely werewolves will dominate in CQC even with very little investment. Indeed one has to purposefully build away from combat to make a Werewolf bad at CQC.</div> </div> </div> </div>(I removed the spoilers because I don't frequent these forums often and didn't know if quoting 100% would produce a wall.)<br /> <br /> Holy cow this is amazing!<br /> <br /> Love the summary at the end that pulls it all together. I think you've <i>thoroughly</i> answered my question at this point.<br /> <br /> I didn't even know dice pools got much bigger than 20, so seeing 40+ is bananas to me.<br /> <br /> I'll let a buddy know he can still be a CQC monster even as a mage!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T19:30:12-08:00","id":1043816,"title":"","content":"Less intensive investment would be the Rote action Dodge from Acceleration that Pendragon suggested to pretty much guarantee you can dodge the werewolf and then use Mind Armor. Even if you lose most CoW the werewolf still can't touch you and you only need to win the CoW once to take him out. If yi feel it's a bit of a dick move to win by dodging without ever landing a blow then use Space armor instead and your dodges will jiu jitsu his own blows back at him plus some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T19:47:35-08:00","id":1043822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043769#post1043769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy cow this is amazing!<br /> <br /> Love the summary at the end that pulls it all together. I think you've <i>thoroughly</i> answered my question at this point.<br /> <br /> I didn't even know dice pools got much bigger than 20, so seeing 40+ is bananas to me.<br /> <br /> I'll let a buddy know he can still be a CQC monster even as a mage!</div> </div> </div> </div>You can be a CQC monster as any splat, you just have to play to their strengths. Mage's strength is prepping up absurdly high dicepools, and using guaranteed reality-fu (time travel, gravity manipulation, hopping into the twilight, etc.) to trump their opponents. Indeed, as a rule of thumb Mages can do just about anything if they dedicate their dots and time to it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043816#post1043816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less intensive investment would be the Rote action Dodge from Acceleration that Pendragon suggested to pretty much guarantee you can dodge the werewolf and then use Mind Armor. Even if you lose most CoW the werewolf still can't touch you and you only need to win the CoW once to take him out. If yi feel it's a bit of a dick move to win by dodging without ever landing a blow then use Space armor instead and your dodges will jiu jitsu his own blows back at him plus some.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd not considered adding Space Armor to the mess, though I'd never allow it to turn the attack back on the attacker. It could however make for a genuine pack killer, or at the very least force the Werewolves to abandon group tactics, as attempt to harm the Mage only result in harming themselves and others.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T21:19:36-08:00","id":1043847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043822#post1043822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can be a CQC monster as any splat, you just have to play to their strengths. Mage's strength is prepping up absurdly high dicepools, and using guaranteed reality-fu (time travel, gravity manipulation, hopping into the twilight, etc.) to trump their opponents. Indeed, as a rule of thumb Mages can do just about anything if they dedicate their dots and time to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd not considered adding Space Armor to the mess, though I'd never allow it to turn the attack back on the attacker. It could however make for a genuine pack killer, or at the very least force the Werewolves to abandon group tactics, as attempt to harm the Mage only result in harming themselves and others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not allow space mage armor to do that? I mean, that's literally what it says you can do, and it costs mana to do so anyways. You don't have to have a missile to cause something to bend back at the attacker.<br /> <br /> Pretty cool builds, though. I didn't realize that dice pools could get that large either. Of course, I prefer the &quot;I cast this one spell on an area that screws you all over&quot; method of fighting over hand to hand. However, it's interesting to see what it might look like if someone did go that route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T21:44:29-08:00","id":1043857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1043847#post1043847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not allow space mage armor to do that? I mean, that's literally what it says you can do, and it costs mana to do so anyways. You don't have to have a missile to cause something to bend back at the attacker.<br /> <br /> Pretty cool builds, though. I didn't realize that dice pools could get that large either. Of course, I prefer the &amp;quot;I cast this one spell on an area that screws you all over&amp;quot; method of fighting over hand to hand. However, it's interesting to see what it might look like if someone did go that route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically because Space Armor says it can redirect to an applicable target, and but this comes down to a storyteller call either way so there's no point arguing it. And yeah, area wide touch of death spells are generally more reliable, but CofD isn't a combat simulator so and there is something undeniably bad ass about laying low five Werewolves in one turn with some sticks on a chain. <br /> <br /> Basically, Mage welcomes all comers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T08:07:13-08:00","id":1044515,"title":"","content":"You could do what my Moros did in the game I'm playing. He has a suit of armor made of overlapping Siderite scales(harder than any mundane material, cannot be breached except by Siderite), with an undersuit of Perfected Leather(can be cut or shot, but perfectly absorbs any bludgeoning attack) and proceeded to go to town. He used Craftsman's Eye(Matter 1) to gain 8-again on attacks with his gauntlets, Crucible(Matter 3) to increase the equipment bonus from his gauntlets to an insane degree and gain the Rote action quality with the same, Aegis(Matter 3) to boost his armor rating to a truly insane degree(not that this matters by the RAW, since Siderite is impenetrable and Perfected Leather perfectly absorbs whatever impacts might shake him up otherwise).<br /> <br /> All of this with an out-of-the-box Moros starting with Gnosis 3 and Matter 3, and access to an Avernian Gate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","name":"CarnivalCash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:15:03-08:00","id":1044551,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest threat to the moros armour build is probably werewolves with the fire elemental gift. <br /> <br /> But I guess the best counter for a mage getting werewolfy <i>would </i>be a werewolf getting mage-y.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:20:28-08:00","id":1044554,"title":"","content":"Or Shaping.<br /> <br /> Plus it's an easy mistake but equipment bonuses aren't the same as weapon bonuses.<br /> <br /> Basically a lot's going to depend on whether you're playing the other character with preptime, too. Or at least playing them smart, something often not done with antagonists, and always a one-sided thing in white rooms. Another suite of problems with the whole white room battle idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-06-2017, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:31:27-08:00","id":1044565,"title":"","content":"I mean, the biggest thing is that you'll almost never be fighting <i>one</i> werewolf. <br /> <br /> But I guess you don't often fight just one mage either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T23:43:52-08:00","id":1044942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1044551#post1044551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the biggest threat to the moros armour build is probably werewolves with the fire elemental gift.<br /> <br /> But I guess the best counter for a mage getting werewolfy <i>would </i>be a werewolf getting mage-y.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's any hint that this is a possibility, simply add Apeiron to the mix for perfect shielding from both heat and radiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","name":"CarnivalCash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T06:07:00-08:00","id":1045010,"title":"","content":"So, watch out for the phrases &quot;Rahu Bone Shadow&quot; and &quot;Meninna Ithaeur&quot; then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T10:39:21-08:00","id":1045216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CarnivalCash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1044515#post1044515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could do what my Moros did in the game I'm playing. He has a suit of armor made of overlapping Siderite scales(harder than any mundane material, cannot be breached except by Siderite), with an undersuit of Perfected Leather(can be cut or shot, but perfectly absorbs any bludgeoning attack) and proceeded to go to town. He used Craftsman's Eye(Matter 1) to gain 8-again on attacks with his gauntlets, Crucible(Matter 3) to increase the equipment bonus from his gauntlets to an insane degree and gain the Rote action quality with the same, Aegis(Matter 3) to boost his armor rating to a truly insane degree(not that this matters by the RAW, since Siderite is impenetrable and Perfected Leather perfectly absorbs whatever impacts might shake him up otherwise).<br /> <br /> All of this with an out-of-the-box Moros starting with Gnosis 3 and Matter 3, and access to an Avernian Gate.</div> </div> </div> </div>please enlighten me, how does crucible boost his dice pool insanely? ... all I can see from the description is that you could give it 8 again along with rote quality, no where do I see you can increase the dicepool with it :S","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12871-elggur","name":"Elggur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T22:12:01-08:00","id":1045616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elggur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043167-can-a-mage-evenly-match-a-werewolf-in-melee-or-hand-to-hand-combat?p=1045216#post1045216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> please enlighten me, how does crucible boost his dice pool insanely? ... all I can see from the description is that you could give it 8 again along with rote quality, no where do I see you can increase the dicepool with it :S</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Right you are. I must have mixed it up with another spell. I really thought Matter was able to increase equipment bonuses. Still, Rote action is perhaps even better than simply boosting its equipment bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","name":"CarnivalCash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T02:47:57-08:00","id":1045661,"title":"","content":"Mages also get very easy access to Steadfast Condition (to the point where they can apply it reflexively). Get yourself a Heavy Weapon Style, pump your dicepool with your favorite dice pump trick, burn all of your dice for Damage Rating using Heavy Weapon Style, and burn Steadfast to make it a certain hit. Heavy Weapon Style Weapon Rating pump lasts for the whole turn, too, so combined with Warding Stance it will also give you tons of Brawl/Weaponry Armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 02-08-2017, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com